🚽 Test case: #193 -- assigning a wrong-tag call result to a struct
🚽 pointer (`p = get_rect(&rc);`) is rejected, the assignment-site
🚽 counterpart of the return-relay tag check.
gang Point { rizz x; };
gang Rect  { rizz w; };
gang Rect  *get_rect(gang Rect *r) { bussin r; }
skibidi main {
    gang Rect rc; rc.w = 1;
    gang Point *p;
    p = get_rect(&rc);
    yapping("%d", p.x);
}
